---
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import EmailReveal from '../../components/EmailReveal.astro';
import { site } from '../../config/site';
import { link } from '../../lib/url';

const toc = [
  { id: 'commitment', title: 'Our approach' },
  { id: 'practices', title: 'What we have done' },
  { id: 'testing', title: 'How it is tested' },
  { id: 'limits', title: 'Known limitations' },
  { id: 'report', title: 'Reporting a problem' },
];

const websiteIssueUrl = `${site.repository}/issues/new?template=website-issue.yml`;
---

<LegalLayout
  doc="accessibility"
  description="How the APOLLO Network website approaches accessibility, how it is tested, its known limitations, and how to report a problem."
  lead="This website should work for everyone who visits it — whatever device, browser, input method or assistive technology they use. Here is where it stands, honestly."
  toc={toc}
>
  <section id="commitment" aria-labelledby="commitment-title">
    <h2 id="commitment-title">Our approach</h2>
    <p>
      We aim to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2 at level AA. Accessibility
      is built into how the site is designed and tested, rather than checked at the end. The site
      has not been formally audited or certified, and we do not claim full conformance.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="practices" aria-labelledby="practices-title">
    <h2 id="practices-title">What we have done</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Everything can be used with a keyboard, with a visible focus indicator and a “skip to
        content” link on every page.
      </li>
      <li>
        Pages use semantic HTML: landmarks, a single main heading, and a logical heading structure.
      </li>
      <li>
        Text colours are chosen for contrast against the dark background, and meaning is never
        carried by colour alone.
      </li>
      <li>
        If your device is set to reduce motion, animations stop: the network visual on the home page
        becomes a still image and content appears without transitions.
      </li>
      <li>
        Layouts are designed for screens from small phones to large desktops, and text can be
        resized.
      </li>
      <li>The site works without JavaScript; only optional extras need it.</li>
      <li>
        Decorative visuals are hidden from screen readers; informative diagrams have text
        alternatives.
      </li>
      <li>
        The APOLLO assistant can be opened, used and closed with a keyboard, and <kbd>Esc</kbd>{' '}
        closes it.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="testing" aria-labelledby="testing-title">
    <h2 id="testing-title">How it is tested</h2>
    <p>
      Every page is checked with automated accessibility testing (axe-core, against WCAG 2.2 AA
      rules) in more than one browser engine, at desktop and mobile sizes. Keyboard navigation,
      reduced-motion behaviour and layouts from 320 pixels wide upwards are checked in Chromium,
      Firefox and WebKit before release.
    </p>
    <p>
      Automated tools catch many problems, but not all of them. That is why your reports matter.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="limits" aria-labelledby="limits-title">
    <h2 id="limits-title">Known limitations</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        The site has not yet been tested by disabled users, or with a full range of screen readers
        and other assistive technologies.
      </li>
      <li>
        Testing has been done in desktop browser engines at mobile screen sizes, not yet on a range
        of physical phones and tablets.
      </li>
      <li>
        Pages linked from this site, such as GitHub, are outside our control and may have their own
        accessibility issues.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="report" aria-labelledby="report-title">
    <h2 id="report-title">Reporting a problem</h2>
    <p>
      If something on this website is hard to use, or you need information in a different format,
      please tell us: <EmailReveal /> You can also use the{' '}
      <a href={link('contact/')}>contact page</a>, or report it publicly with the{' '}
      <a href={websiteIssueUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer external">
        website problem form<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens external site)</span>
      </a>
      .
    </p>
    <p>
      It helps to include the page address, what you were trying to do, and the device, browser and
      any assistive technology you use. We will do our best to fix the problem or find another way
      to get you the information.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalLayout>
